---
// src/pages/managed-noc.astro
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="24/7 NOC & Managed Network Operations | InfraHub"
  description="Evaluate partner-delivered 24/7 NOC coverage, network engineering, automation, and AI-assisted operations for connectivity and infrastructure teams."
  canonicalPath="/managed-noc"
>
  <div class="section section-hero network-overlay">
    <div class="container service-container">
      <div class="service-header">
        <div class="header-badge-row">
          <span class="pill-badge badge-blue">Operational Resilience</span>
          <span class="pill-badge badge-teal">Partner Delivered</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="service-title">24/7 NOC & Managed Operations</h1>
        <p class="service-lead">
          Extend your internal team with continuous monitoring, incident triage, network engineering, source-of-truth-driven automation, and AI-assisted operational workflows delivered by a specialist provider.
        </p>
        <div class="service-hero-actions">
          <a href="/lets-talk?service=managed-noc" class="btn btn-accent btn-lg">Request NOC Coverage Evaluation</a>
          <a href="#coverage-models" class="btn btn-secondary btn-lg">Review Coverage Models</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="content-section" id="coverage-models">
        <span class="section-sub-tag">The Operating Model</span>
        <h2>When External NOC Coverage Can Help</h2>
        <p>
          Running genuine round-the-clock operations internally means covering nights, weekends, holidays, escalation, documentation, and continuity when key engineers are unavailable. A managed model can take responsibility for defined operating windows or incident classes while the buyer retains ownership of architecture and policy.
        </p>
        <div class="problem-grid">
          <div class="problem-card">
            <h3>Coverage Continuity</h3>
            <p>Maintain monitoring and first response outside the internal team's normal operating hours without depending on informal on-call arrangements.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="problem-card">
            <h3>Defined Escalation</h3>
            <p>Separate routine triage from issues that need senior network engineers, with documented handoff and escalation paths agreed in advance.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="problem-card">
            <h3>Operational Discipline</h3>
            <p>Use repeatable runbooks, ticketing, maintenance procedures, and source-of-truth data so response does not depend on one person's memory.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="content-section">
        <span class="section-sub-tag">Coverage Models</span>
        <h2>Common Managed Operations Scopes</h2>
        <div class="noc-tiers-grid">
          <div class="noc-tier-card">
            <span class="tier-pill">Monitoring & Triage</span>
            <h3>Alert Review & Runbook Execution</h3>
            <p>Continuous monitoring, incident classification, ticket creation, communication, and execution of pre-approved operational procedures.</p>
            <ul class="tier-features">
              <li>Monitoring and alert acknowledgement</li>
              <li>Ticket and escalation workflow</li>
              <li>Pre-approved runbook actions</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="noc-tier-card">
            <span class="tier-pill">Engineering</span>
            <h3>Network & Infrastructure Escalation</h3>
            <p>Hands-on troubleshooting across routing, switching, connectivity, virtual infrastructure, and the systems surrounding the network.</p>
            <ul class="tier-features">
              <li>Carrier and circuit troubleshooting</li>
              <li>BGP, peering, and routing investigation</li>
              <li>Escalation to senior engineering when required</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="noc-tier-card highlight-tier">
            <span class="tier-pill tier-ai">Automation & AI</span>
            <h3>AI-Assisted Network Operations</h3>
            <p>Use source-of-truth-driven automation and AI-assisted workflows to add context to incidents, reduce repetitive work, and help engineers move from reactive handling toward more proactive operations.</p>
            <ul class="tier-features">
              <li>Operational context and alert correlation</li>
              <li>Automation around repeatable network tasks</li>
              <li>Workflow support for investigation and remediation</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="content-section">
        <div class="infrahub-role-card">
          <span class="pill-badge badge-teal">Partner Ecosystem</span>
          <h2>ITcare for Network Engineering & Operations</h2>
          <p>
            ITcare designs, builds, and operates production networks for ISPs, data-center operators, and cloud and hosting providers. Its published service portfolio covers network architecture and engineering, infrastructure support, 24/7 NOC operations, DevOps and automation, and AI NetOps through HORA.
          </p>
          <div class="role-points-grid">
            <div class="role-point">
              <h3><a href="/partners/itcare">Network Engineering</a></h3>
              <p>Architecture and operational support across technologies including BGP, MPLS, EVPN-VXLAN, peering, and IP transit.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="role-point">
              <h3>24/7 NOC</h3>
              <p>Round-the-clock monitoring, incident detection, response, and escalation for production infrastructure.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="role-point">
              <h3>Automation & HORA</h3>
              <p>Infrastructure automation plus AI-assisted NetOps workflows intended to reduce repetitive handling and improve operational context.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="service-footer-cta">
        <h2>Define the Coverage You Actually Need</h2>
        <p>Start with operating hours, monitored systems, escalation boundaries, tooling, and the responsibilities you want a provider to own.</p>
        <a href="/lets-talk?service=managed-noc" class="btn btn-accent btn-lg">Discuss Managed Operations</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .service-container { max-width: 1040px; }
  .service-header { text-align: left; max-width: 860px; margin: 0 0 64px; padding-bottom: 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color); }
  .header-badge-row { display: flex; justify-content: flex-start; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .service-title { font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4vw, 3.4rem); font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.15; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .service-lead { font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.65; margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .service-hero-actions { display: flex; justify-content: flex-start; gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .content-section { margin-bottom: 72px; }
  .section-sub-tag { display: block; font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--accent-blue); margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .content-section h2 { font-size: 1.85rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .content-section > p { font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.65; max-width: 780px; margin-bottom: 28px; }

  .problem-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 20px; }
  @media (min-width: 768px) { .problem-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
  .problem-card { background-color: var(--bg-secondary); border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 24px; }
  .problem-card h3 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 10px; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .problem-card p { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5; }

  .noc-tiers-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px; }
  @media (min-width: 768px) { .noc-tiers-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
  .noc-tier-card { background-color: #ffffff; border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 28px; box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm); display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .highlight-tier { border-color: var(--accent-blue); background-color: var(--accent-blue-light); }
  .tier-pill { display: inline-block; font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: var(--accent-teal); margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .tier-ai { color: var(--accent-blue); }
  .noc-tier-card h3 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .noc-tier-card p { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .tier-features { list-style: disc; padding-left: 18px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-secondary); }

  .infrahub-role-card { background-color: var(--bg-dark); color: #ffffff; border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 44px 36px; }
  .infrahub-role-card h2 { color: #ffffff; margin: 12px 0 16px; }
  .infrahub-role-card > p { color: var(--text-on-dark-muted); font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .role-points-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px; }
  @media (min-width: 768px) { .role-points-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
  .role-point { background-color: transparent; border: none; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12); border-radius: 0; padding: 18px 0 0; }
  .role-point h3 { color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .role-point h3 a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
  .role-point h3 a:hover { color: #93c5fd; }
  .role-point p { color: var(--text-on-dark-muted); font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.5; }

  .service-footer-cta { padding: 40px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; text-align: left; gap: 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color); }
</style>
